s (e.g., W1 or T3) reduces flexibility. Among honors, F3 (West Wind) has the lowest value since it is neither seat wind (East/F1) nor prevalent wind (South), making it the best candidate for discard. Discarding F3 preserves F1 for potential Seat Wind pattern (2 points) and avoids weakening suited meld opportunities.\n\nReason: Discarding F3 removes a dead tile with no chow potential, increasing the likelihood of drawing suited tiles needed for Mixed Triple Chow (which alone satisfies the 8-point minimum). Keeping F1 leverages seat wind advantage, while discarding suited tiles like W1 or T3 would unnecessarily sacrifice chow components (e.g., W1 only fits 123, limiting options). Honor discards are statistically safer early-game due to lower honor tile prevalence (28 vs. 108 suited tiles), and F3 specifically lacks strategic value compared to F1.\n\nAnswer: Play F3"}
